IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ea-part2`
IMPORT `ea-part2-continuity`
IMPORT `ea-part3-salary`
IMPORT `ea-part4-hours`
IMPORT `ea-part9-maternity`
IMPORT `ea-part10-leave`
IMPORT `ea-part12-records`
IMPORT `ea-part12-retrenchment`
IMPORT `ea-retrenchment-reporting-notification`

-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal
-- consolidation in force from 5 December 2025 -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: the employee (one person, in one employment with one employer).
--
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the modules imported above
-- as the questions an employee would ask about their own job: how much notice
-- they are owed, whether they can be dismissed or suspended, when they must be
-- paid, what may be deducted, what their rest days, overtime and leave are
-- worth, what maternity protection they have, and what their employer must
-- give them or report. Nothing here is new law.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS (21 October 2026). Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no,
-- numbers and the modules' own choices -- one for each fact the employee
-- states, each with an @desc worded as the employee would be asked ("Does
-- your contract say how much notice must be given?"). The records the long
-- modules expect (ContractTerms, ServiceLength, Absence ...) are built inside
-- each question, in its WHERE, from those answers, and the SAME module rule is
-- then called; no rule is restated here. A record field that the rule called
-- never reads is given a fixed placeholder, with a comment saying so. Fields a
-- rule does read are always asked, except the figures the Minister may
-- substitute: the s 29 proportion, the s 35 salary thresholds and the s 95A
-- deadline are taken as the Act states them (the modules' own constants), so
-- a later Ministerial substitution would change these answers.
-- The employer's seat is a separate layer beside this one,
-- ea-seat-employer.l4, over the same modules.
--
-- Where the existing encoding departs from the defaults ruled on 2026-10-18
-- (recorded, not fixed, in this pass):
--   * Most rules are phrased from the employer's or the Commissioner's side
--     ("the employer has complied with section 95(1)", "section 38(1)(a) was
--     contravened", "employing this child contravenes section 68(1)"); this
--     layer re-phrases the main ones and leaves the rest as they are.
--   * Judgments the Act leaves to someone else are taken as plain facts rather
--     than answered conditionally: whether the employee had a "reasonable
--     excuse" (s 13(2)), whether the employer held a "due inquiry" and there was
--     misconduct (s 14(1)), whether danger is "immediate" (s 15), whether work is
--     "light work suited to the child's capacity" (s 68(3)).
--   * Enforcement machinery is encoded beside the operative rules: the s 96A
--     administrative penalties, contravention notices, reconsideration and
--     directions (ss 126A-126D), the secrecy provisions (ss 101-102), and the
--     s 82 offence.
--   * The instruments that set the Act's prescribed numbers (record retention,
--     pay slip timing, the Fifth Schedule, the s 95A minimum period) were not
--     retrieved, so those numbers are supplied facts; only the Retrenchment
--     Reporting Notification 2019 is brought in.
--   * Length of service under s 10(3) is asked band by band rather than
--     worked out from dates (see NOTES.md, observation 2).

§ `Employment Act 1968 -- the employee's questions`

§§ `Notice, and leaving the job`

-- ss 8, 10(2), 10(3). "Notice" is the warning either side must give to end
-- the contract of service. The contract's figure governs unless it is shorter
-- than the Act's minimum for the employee's length of service, in which case
-- s 8 voids it and the Act's minimum applies.
@export How many days of notice am I owed (ss 8, 10(2), 10(3))?
GIVEN `my contract sets the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your contract say how much notice must be given?
      `my contract's notice in days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days' notice does your contract give? (0 if it says nothing)
      `I have worked 26 weeks or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you worked for this employer for 26 weeks or more?
      `I have worked 2 years or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you worked for this employer for 2 years or more?
      `I have worked 5 years or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you worked for this employer for 5 years or more?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days of notice am I owed` IS
    `the notice period that governs, in days` `my terms` `my service`
    WHERE
        `my terms` MEANS ContractTerms WITH
            `the contract makes provision for notice` IS `my contract sets the notice`
            `the notice period the contract provides, in days` IS `my contract's notice in days`
            -- Placeholder: the notice period rule does not read this field.
            `the contract provides the same length for both parties` IS TRUE
        `my service` MEANS ServiceLength WITH
            `employed for 26 weeks or more` IS `I have worked 26 weeks or more`
            `employed for 2 years or more` IS `I have worked 2 years or more`
            `employed for 5 years or more` IS `I have worked 5 years or more`

-- s 11(1). "Salary in lieu of notice": instead of notice, a party may end the
-- contract by paying the salary, at the gross rate of pay (pay before
-- deductions), that would have accrued over the notice period.
@export How much must I be paid in lieu of notice, in dollars (s 11(1))?
GIVEN `my contract sets the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your contract say how much notice must be given?
      `my contract's notice in days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days' notice does your contract give? (0 if it says nothing)
      `I have worked 26 weeks or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you worked for this employer for 26 weeks or more?
      `I have worked 2 years or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you worked for this employer for 2 years or more?
      `I have worked 5 years or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you worked for this employer for 5 years or more?
      `my gross daily pay` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your gross pay for one day, before deductions, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much must I be paid in lieu of notice` IS
    `the payment in lieu of notice` `my gross daily pay` `my terms` `my service`
    WHERE
        `my terms` MEANS ContractTerms WITH
            `the contract makes provision for notice` IS `my contract sets the notice`
            `the notice period the contract provides, in days` IS `my contract's notice in days`
            -- Placeholder: the payment in lieu rule does not read this field.
            `the contract provides the same length for both parties` IS TRUE
        `my service` MEANS ServiceLength WITH
            `employed for 26 weeks or more` IS `I have worked 26 weeks or more`
            `employed for 2 years or more` IS `I have worked 2 years or more`
            `employed for 5 years or more` IS `I have worked 5 years or more`

-- s 13(2). "Deemed to have broken the contract": treated by the Act as having
-- ended the contract by breach, as if the employee had walked out. Absence of
-- more than 2 days continuously, without prior leave, and either no reasonable
-- excuse or no attempt to tell the employer of it.
@export Am I treated as having broken my contract by being absent from work (s 13(2))?
GIVEN `days I was absent in a row` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days in a row were you absent from work?
      `I had leave beforehand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer give you leave for the absence beforehand?
      `I had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a reasonable excuse for being absent?
      `I told my employer why` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you tell your employer, or try to, why you were absent?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as having broken my contract by being absent` IF
    `the employee is deemed to have broken the contract` `my absence`
    WHERE
        `my absence` MEANS Absence WITH
            `days absent continuously` IS `days I was absent in a row`
            `with prior leave from the employer` IS `I had leave beforehand`
            `the employee has a reasonable excuse for the absence` IS `I had a reasonable excuse`
            `the employee informed or attempted to inform the employer of the excuse` IS `I told my employer why`

-- s 15. An employee may end the contract without notice if they or their
-- dependant are threatened with immediate danger to the person by violence or
-- disease which they did not undertake to run by the contract of service.
@export May I leave my job without notice because of danger (s 15)?
GIVEN `the threat is to me or my dependant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the danger to you, or to someone who depends on you?
      `the danger is immediate to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the danger immediate?
      `the danger is to my person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a danger to the person (to body or life, not to property)?
      `the danger is from violence or disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the danger come from violence or disease?
      `my contract made me run that risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you agree in your contract of service to run that risk?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I leave without notice because of danger` IF
    `the employee may terminate without notice under section 15` `my danger`
    WHERE
        `my danger` MEANS DangerFacts WITH
            `the threat is to the employee or the employee's dependant` IS `the threat is to me or my dependant`
            `the danger is immediate` IS `the danger is immediate to me`
            `the danger is to the person` IS `the danger is to my person`
            `the danger is by violence or disease` IS `the danger is from violence or disease`
            `the employee undertook by the contract of service to run that risk` IS `my contract made me run that risk`

§§ `Dismissal and suspension`

-- s 14(1). "Due inquiry": a proper inquiry by the employer into the alleged
-- misconduct before acting on it. "Misconduct inconsistent with the conditions
-- of service": conduct that breaks the express or implied terms of the job.
@export Can my employer dismiss me without notice for misconduct (s 14(1))?
GIVEN `I committed misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you commit misconduct that goes against the express or implied terms of your job?
      `my employer held a due inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer first hold a proper inquiry (a "due inquiry") into it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my employer dismiss me without notice for misconduct` IF
    `the employer may dismiss without notice under section 14(1)` `my dismissal facts`
    WHERE
        `my dismissal facts` MEANS DismissalFacts WITH
            `there was misconduct inconsistent with the conditions of service` IS `I committed misconduct`
            `the employer held a due inquiry` IS `my employer held a due inquiry`
            -- Placeholders: the s 14(1) dismissal rule does not read these fields.
            `the employee was instead down-graded` IS FALSE
            `the employee was instead suspended without salary` IS FALSE
            `the days of suspension` IS 0

-- s 14(1)(b). Instead of dismissing, the employer may suspend without salary
-- for a period not exceeding one week, after the same due inquiry.
@export Is my suspension without pay lawful (s 14(1)(b))?
GIVEN `I committed misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you commit misconduct that goes against the express or implied terms of your job?
      `my employer held a due inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer first hold a proper inquiry (a "due inquiry") into it?
      `I was suspended without pay instead` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you suspended without pay instead of being dismissed?
      `days I was suspended` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days were you suspended for?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my suspension without pay lawful` IF
    `the suspension is lawful under section 14(1)(b)` `my suspension facts`
    WHERE
        `my suspension facts` MEANS DismissalFacts WITH
            `there was misconduct inconsistent with the conditions of service` IS `I committed misconduct`
            `the employer held a due inquiry` IS `my employer held a due inquiry`
            -- Placeholder: the s 14(1)(b) suspension rule does not read this field.
            `the employee was instead down-graded` IS FALSE
            `the employee was instead suspended without salary` IS `I was suspended without pay instead`
            `the days of suspension` IS `days I was suspended`

-- s 14(2A). Only a "relevant employee" may claim for wrongful dismissal: any
-- employee not in a managerial or executive position; a manager or executive
-- dismissed without notice and without salary in lieu; or a manager or
-- executive dismissed with notice (or salary in lieu) after 6 months' service.
@export Can I claim for wrongful dismissal (s 14(2A))?
GIVEN `I was a manager or executive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you in a managerial or executive position?
      `I was dismissed with notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you dismissed with notice?
      `I was paid in lieu of notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you dismissed without notice but paid salary in place of notice?
      `I served 6 months or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had you worked for this employer for at least 6 months, in any position?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I claim for wrongful dismissal` IF
    `the employee may lodge a wrongful dismissal claim` `me as dismissed`
    WHERE
        `me as dismissed` MEANS Dismissed WITH
            `in a managerial or an executive position` IS `I was a manager or executive`
            `dismissed with notice` IS `I was dismissed with notice`
            `dismissed without notice but paid salary in lieu` IS `I was paid in lieu of notice`
            `served that employer for at least 6 months in any position` IS `I served 6 months or more`

-- s 45. "Retrenchment benefit": a payment on dismissal for redundancy or
-- reorganisation. Under 2 years' continuous service, the Act says none is
-- owed.
@export Am I barred from a retrenchment benefit because my service was too short (s 45)?
GIVEN `I was dismissed for redundancy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you dismissed because of redundancy or a reorganisation of the business?
      `my years of continuous service` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years of continuous service do you have with this employer?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I barred from a retrenchment benefit by my short service` IF
    `section 45 bars any retrenchment benefit` `my service for benefits`
    WHERE
        `my service for benefits` MEANS ServiceForBenefits WITH
            `years of continuous service with the employer` IS `my years of continuous service`
            `dismissed on the ground of redundancy or by reason of a reorganisation` IS `I was dismissed for redundancy`
            -- Placeholder: the s 45 rule does not read this field (s 46 does).
            `the service has ceased` IS TRUE

§§ `Being paid`

-- ss 21 to 23. Salary must be paid within 7 days after the salary period, 14
-- days for overtime, 3 days after a dismissal, on the day the contract ends
-- after due notice, and within 7 days where the employee leaves without notice.
@export Was I paid late (ss 21 to 23)?
GIVEN `the occasion` IS A PaymentOccasion @desc What was the payment for?
      `the days taken to pay` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after the end of the salary period (or after the dismissal or the end of the contract) were you paid?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was I paid late` IF
    `the payment was late` `the occasion` `the days taken to pay`

-- ss 27 and 32 with s 27(1)(d)-(e) and (i). An "authorised deduction" is one the
-- Act lists; some of them need the employee's written consent, which the
-- employee may withdraw in writing before the deduction is made.
@export Can my employer make this deduction from my salary (ss 26, 27)?
GIVEN `the kind` IS A DeductionKind @desc What is the deduction for?
      `I consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give your written consent to the deduction?
      `I withdrew my consent in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you withdraw that consent in writing before the deduction was made?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my employer make this deduction from my salary` IF
    `the deduction may lawfully be made` `the kind` `my consent`
    WHERE
        `my consent` MEANS Consent WITH
            `written consent was given` IS `I consented in writing`
            `written notice of withdrawal was given before the deduction was made` IS `I withdrew my consent in writing`

-- s 29. A deduction for damage or loss caused by the employee's neglect or
-- default: no more than the loss, no more than a quarter of a month's wages
-- unless the Commissioner (the Commissioner for Labour) permits more, and only
-- after the employee has had a chance to "show cause" (explain why it should
-- not be made).
@export Can my employer deduct this amount for damage or loss I caused (s 29)?
GIVEN `the loss I caused` IS A NUMBER @desc How much damage or loss did your neglect or default cause, in dollars?
      `my month's wages` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your wages for one month, in dollars?
      `the amount to be deducted` IS A NUMBER @desc How much does your employer want to deduct, in dollars?
      `the Commissioner permitted more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commissioner for Labour permitted a larger deduction?
      `I had a chance to show cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you given a chance to explain why the deduction should not be made?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my employer deduct this amount for damage or loss I caused` IF
    `the damages deduction may be made` `my damages deduction` `the proportions as the Act states them`
    WHERE
        `my damages deduction` MEANS DamagesDeduction WITH
            `the amount of the damages or loss caused by the employee's neglect or default` IS `the loss I caused`
            `one month's wages` IS `my month's wages`
            `the amount the employer proposes to deduct` IS `the amount to be deducted`
            `the Commissioner has permitted a larger deduction` IS `the Commissioner permitted more`
            `the employee has been given an opportunity of showing cause` IS `I had a chance to show cause`
        -- The proportion is the Act's own (one quarter), not asked.

§§ `Hours, rest days and overtime`

-- s 35. Part 4 (rest days, hours, overtime) covers a "workman" (an employee
-- doing mainly manual labour) earning up to $4,500 a month, and any other
-- employee earning up to $2,600 a month, but not managers or executives.
@export Do the rest day, hours and overtime rules in Part 4 cover me (s 35)?
GIVEN `I am a workman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your work mainly manual labour (are you a "workman")?
      `I am a manager or executive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in a managerial or executive position?
      `my basic monthly salary` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic monthly salary, leaving out overtime, bonus, annual wage supplement, productivity incentive and allowances, in dollars?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the rest day, hours and overtime rules cover me` IF
    `this Part applies to the employee` `me as a worker` `the caps as the Act states them`
    WHERE
        `me as a worker` MEANS Worker WITH
            `is a workman` IS `I am a workman`
            `is employed in a managerial or an executive position` IS `I am a manager or executive`
            `monthly salary excluding overtime, bonus, annual wage supplement, productivity incentive and allowances` IS `my basic monthly salary`
        -- The thresholds are the Act's own ($4,500 and $2,600), not asked.

-- s 37. The pay for working on a "rest day" (the employee's one whole day off
-- a week), which doubles where the work was at the employer's request.
@export What must I be paid for working on my rest day, in dollars (s 37)?
GIVEN `I asked to work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you work on your rest day at your own request (rather than your employer's)?
      `hours I worked on the rest day` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours did you work on your rest day?
      `my usual hours were agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you and your employer agreed your usual hours of work per day?
      `my agreed usual hours` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many hours a day? (0 if not agreed)
      `my basic daily pay` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic pay for one day's work, in dollars?
      `my hourly basic pay` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic pay per hour, without allowances, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What must I be paid for working on my rest day` IS
    `the payment for working on the rest day` `my rest day work`
    WHERE
        `my rest day work` MEANS RestDayWork WITH
            `hours agreed as the usual hours of work per day were agreed` IS `my usual hours were agreed`
            `the agreed usual hours of work per day` IS `my agreed usual hours`
            `the hours actually worked on the rest day` IS `hours I worked on the rest day`
            `the basic rate of pay for one day's work` IS `my basic daily pay`
            `the hourly basic rate of pay` IS `my hourly basic pay`
            `the work was at the employee's own request` IS `I asked to work`

-- s 38(4). Overtime is paid at not less than one and a half times the
-- "hourly basic rate of pay" (basic pay, without allowances, per hour).
@export What is my overtime pay, in dollars (s 38(4))?
GIVEN `the extra hours` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of overtime did you work?
      `the hourly basic rate of pay` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic pay per hour, without allowances, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my overtime pay` IS
    `the overtime payment` `the extra hours` `the hourly basic rate of pay`

§§ `Leave`

-- s 88A. "Annual leave": paid leave, 7 days in the first year of service, one
-- more day each year to 14; pro-rated in a part year; nothing under 3 months'
-- service, and lost entirely for absence without permission or reasonable
-- excuse on more than 20% of working days.
@export How many days of paid annual leave do I get this year (s 88A)?
GIVEN `my complete months of service` IS A NUMBER @desc How many complete months have you worked for this employer?
      `my complete years of service` IS A NUMBER @desc How many complete years (12-month periods) of continuous service do you have with this employer?
      `my complete months this year` IS A NUMBER @desc How many complete months have you worked in this year of service?
      `I was absent on over 20% of days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you absent without permission or reasonable excuse on more than 20% of your working days?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days of annual leave do I get` IS
    `the annual leave days the employee is entitled to` `my leave service`
    WHERE
        `my leave service` MEANS LeaveService WITH
            `completed months of service with the employer` IS `my complete months of service`
            `completed 12 month periods of continuous service` IS `my complete years of service`
            `completed months of service in that year` IS `my complete months this year`
            `absent without permission or reasonable excuse for more than 20% of the working days` IS `I was absent on over 20% of days`

-- s 89. Paid sick leave after examination by a medical practitioner: up to 14
-- days of outpatient sick leave a year, or up to 60 where hospitalisation is
-- necessary, scaled down in the first 6 months of service.
@export How many days of paid sick leave can I take this year (s 89)?
GIVEN `my complete months of service` IS A NUMBER @desc How many complete months have you worked for this employer?
      `a doctor examined me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you examined by a medical practitioner?
      `I need hospitalisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is hospitalisation necessary?
      `days I am in hospital` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days are you hospitalised this year? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days of paid sick leave can I take` IS
    `the paid sick leave ceiling in days` `my sick leave facts`
    WHERE
        `my sick leave facts` MEANS SickLeaveFacts WITH
            `completed months of service with the employer` IS `my complete months of service`
            `examined by a medical practitioner` IS `a doctor examined me`
            `hospitalisation is necessary` IS `I need hospitalisation`
            `days on which the employee is hospitalised` IS `days I am in hospital`

§§ `Maternity`

-- s 76(1A), (2B) and s 83. The "benefit period" is the 8 weeks of the
-- maternity absence that the employer must pay for; it needs 3 months' service
-- before confinement (giving birth), and is forfeited by working for another
-- employer during the absence.
@export Am I entitled to be paid during my maternity benefit period (ss 76, 83)?
GIVEN `I delivered on or after 22 August 2015` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your baby born (or is it expected) on or after 22 August 2015?
      `my months of service before confinement` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months had you worked for this employer before the day you gave birth?
      `I worked for another employer during it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you worked for another employer during your maternity absence?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to be paid during my maternity benefit period` IF
    `she is entitled to payment during the benefit period` `my maternity facts`
    WHERE
        `my maternity facts` MEANS MaternityFacts WITH
            -- Placeholder: the entitlement rule does not read this field.
            `the arrangement` IS `the default -- 4 weeks before and 8 weeks after`
            `delivered on or after 22 August 2015, or with an estimated delivery date on or after that day` IS `I delivered on or after 22 August 2015`
            `months served preceding the day of confinement` IS `my months of service before confinement`
            -- Placeholders: the entitlement rule does not read these fields.
            `the gross rate of pay for one day` IS 0
            `days worked during the benefit period before confinement` IS 0
            `has worked for another employer after absenting herself under this Part` IS `I worked for another employer during it`

-- s 76(1A). The payment is the gross rate of pay for each day of the 8-week
-- benefit period.
@export How much maternity pay do I get, in dollars (s 76(1A))?
GIVEN `how I take my absence` IS AN AbsenceArrangement @desc How are you taking your maternity absence?
      `I delivered on or after 22 August 2015` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your baby born (or is it expected) on or after 22 August 2015?
      `my months of service before confinement` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months had you worked for this employer before the day you gave birth?
      `my gross daily pay` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your gross pay for one day, before deductions, in dollars?
      `I worked for another employer during it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you worked for another employer during your maternity absence?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much maternity pay do I get` IS
    `the payment for the benefit period` `my maternity facts`
    WHERE
        `my maternity facts` MEANS MaternityFacts WITH
            `the arrangement` IS `how I take my absence`
            `delivered on or after 22 August 2015, or with an estimated delivery date on or after that day` IS `I delivered on or after 22 August 2015`
            `months served preceding the day of confinement` IS `my months of service before confinement`
            `the gross rate of pay for one day` IS `my gross daily pay`
            -- Placeholder: the payment rule does not read this field.
            `days worked during the benefit period before confinement` IS 0
            `has worked for another employer after absenting herself under this Part` IS `I worked for another employer during it`

-- s 81. While absent on maternity leave under Part 9, the employer may not
-- give notice of dismissal during the absence, or on a day such that the
-- notice would expire during it.
@export Is the notice of dismissal I was given around my maternity absence unlawful (s 81)?
GIVEN `the employee is absent in accordance with this Part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you absent on maternity leave under Part 9 of the Act?
      `notice of dismissal was given during the absence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you given the notice of dismissal during that absence?
      `the notice would expire during the absence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the notice run out during that absence?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the notice of dismissal I was given during my maternity absence unlawful` IF
    `the notice of dismissal is unlawful under section 81` `the employee is absent in accordance with this Part` `notice of dismissal was given during the absence` `the notice would expire during the absence`

§§ `What my employer must give me or report`

-- s 95A. "Key employment terms": the written record of the main terms of the
-- job, which must be given within 14 days of starting (for contracts made on
-- or after 1 April 2016 and service of at least the prescribed minimum).
@export Has my employer failed to give me my key employment terms in writing in time (s 95A)?
GIVEN `my contract was made after 1 April 2016` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you enter into your contract of service on or after 1 April 2016?
      `I am employed for the prescribed minimum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed for at least the prescribed minimum period of service?
      `I got my key terms in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your employer given you your key employment terms in writing?
      `days after starting I got them` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after you started work did you get them? (0 if never)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my employer failed to give me my key employment terms in time` IF
    `the employer has contravened section 95A` `my key terms facts`
    WHERE
        `my key terms facts` MEANS KeyTermsFacts WITH
            `the contract of service was entered into on or after 1 April 2016` IS `my contract was made after 1 April 2016`
            `employed for a period not shorter than the prescribed minimum period of service` IS `I am employed for the prescribed minimum`
            `a written record of the key employment terms was given` IS `I got my key terms in writing`
            `days after the start of employment when it was given` IS `days after starting I got them`
            -- The seat assumes the Act's own figure: no other deadline is
            -- prescribed, so the 14 days in s 95A(2) govern.
            `another period has been prescribed in substitution` IS FALSE
            `the substituted period in days` IS 0

-- s 96A and the Employment (Retrenchment Reporting) Notification 2019. Where
-- an employer with 10 or more covered employees gives a covered employee
-- notice of "retrenchment" (termination at the employer's initiative for
-- redundancy or reorganisation), it must report it to the Commissioner.
@export Must my employer report my retrenchment to the Commissioner for Labour (s 96A; Retrenchment Reporting Notification 2019, para 3)?
GIVEN `I am an employee under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an "employee" under the Act (working under a contract of service, and not a seafarer or domestic worker)?
      `my contract has an end date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your contract of service say when it ends?
      `my contract's term in months` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many months is it for? (0 if open-ended)
      `my employer's covered employees` IS A NUMBER @desc How many employees covered by the Notification did your employer have on the day you were given notice?
      `my employer ended it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it your employer who decided to end your employment?
      `the reason was redundancy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the reason redundancy or a reorganisation of the business?
      `the day I got notice` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day were you given notice, as a day number (day 0 is Monday 1 November 2021)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my employer report my retrenchment to the Commissioner` IF
    `a retrenchment report must be given for the notice` `my notice of retrenchment`
    WHERE
        `my notice of retrenchment` MEANS `Notice of retrenchment` WITH
            `the person is an employee under section 2(1) of the Act` IS `I am an employee under the Act`
            `the contract` IS `Contract of service` WITH
                `specifies an end date` IS `my contract has an end date`
                `term of employment in months` IS `my contract's term in months`
            `employees within the Notification on the day notice is given` IS `my employer's covered employees`
            `the employer initiated the termination` IS `my employer ended it`
            `the reason is redundancy or a reorganisation` IS `the reason was redundancy`
            `the day the notice is given` IS `the day I got notice`
            -- Placeholder: the para 3 duty does not read this field.
            `the day the notice takes effect` IS `the day I got notice`
